===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*strengʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|string}}, {{m|enm|streng}}, {{m|enm|strynge}}, from {{inh|en|ang|strenġ}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*strangi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*strangiz|t=string}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*strengʰ-|t=rope, cord, strand; to tighten}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|sco|string||string}}, {{cog|nl|streng||cord, strand}}, {{cog|nds|strenge||strand, cord, rope}}, {{cog|de|Strang||strand, cord, rope}}, {{cog|da|streng||string}}, {{cog|sv|sträng||string, cord, wire}}, {{cog|is|strengur||string}}, {{cog|lv|stringt||to be tight, wither}}, {{cog|la|stringō||I tighten}}, {{cog|grc|στραγγαλόομαι||to strangle}}, from {{m|grc|στραγγάλη||halter}}, {{cog|grc|στραγγός||tied together, entangled, twisted}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A long, thin and flexible structure made from [[thread]]s twisted together.
#: {{syn|en|cord|rope|line|thread|Thesaurus:string}}
#* '''1700''', {{w|Matthew Prior}}, ''Carmen Seculare. for the Year 1700''
#*: Round Ormond's knee thou tiest the mystic '''string'''.
#*: {{lb|en|countable}} A thread
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Such a structure considered as a substance.
#: {{syn|en|cord|rope|twine}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A thread.
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any similar long, thin and flexible object.
## {{lb|en|musical instrument}} A segment of [[wire]] (typically made of plastic or metal) or other material used as vibrating element on a [[musical instrument]].
##: {{ux|en|a violin'''string'''}}
##: {{ux|en|a [[bowstring|bow'''string''']]}}
## {{lb|en|sports}} A length of [[nylon]] or other material on the [[head]] of a [[racquet]].
# A [[thread]] or [[cord]] on which a number of objects or [[parts]] are strung or arranged in close and orderly succession; [[hence]], a [[line]] or series of things arranged on a thread, or as if so arranged.
#: {{ux|en|a '''string''' of shells or beads}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''string''' of sausages}}
#* {{RQ:Gibbon Roman Empire
|passage=a '''string''' of islands}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A cohesive substance taking the form of a string.
#: {{ux|en|The '''string''' of spittle dangling from his chin was most unattractive}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A series of items or events.
#: {{syn|en|sequence|series}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Christoper Zara|title=Tortured Artists: From Picasso and Monroe to Warhol and Winehouse, the Twisted Secrets of the World's Most Creative Minds|section=part 1, chapter 1, {{gbooks|q=string|id=HV4jKhjzMVYC|pg=27}}
|passage=In 1933, disgusted and discouraged after a '''string''' of commercial failures, Clara quit the film business forever. She was twenty-six.}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''string''' of successes}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The members of a sports team or squad regarded as most likely to achieve success. (Perhaps metaphorical as the "strings" that hold the squad together.) Often first '''string''', second '''string''' etc.
# {{lb|en|countable}} In various games and competitions, a certain number of turns at play, of rounds, etc.
# {{lb|en|collective}} A [[drove]] of [[horse]]s, or a group of [[racehorse]]s kept by one owner or at one [[stable]].
# {{senseid|en|programming}} {{lb|en|countable|programming}} An ordered sequence of [[text]] [[character]]s stored consecutively in [[memory]] and capable of being processed as a single entity.
# {{lb|en|music|metonym|countable}} A [[stringed instrument]].
# {{lb|en|music|usually|in the plural}} The [[stringed instrument]]s as a section of an orchestra, especially those played by a bow, or the persons playing those instruments.
#: {{syn|en|string section}}
# {{lb|en|figurative|in the plural}} The conditions and limitations in a contract collectively.
#: {{syn|en|conditions|provisions}}
#: {{ux|en|[[no strings attached|no '''strings''' attached]]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 December 14|author=Mel Holley|title=Network News: Strikes go on as RMT rejects RDG's "detrimental" offer|journal=RAIL|issue=972|page=8|text=But he added: "The RDG offer contains more '''strings''' than a harp, including some which have never previously been discussed. It also omits significant points that had previously been negotiated."}}
# {{lb|en|countable|physics}} A tiny one-dimensional string-like entity, the main [[object]] of study in [[string theory]], a branch of [[theoretical physics]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[cannabis|Cannabis]] or [[marijuana]].
# {{lb|en|billiards}} Part of the game of [[billiards]], where the order of the play is determined by testing who can get a ball closest to the bottom [[rail]] by shooting it onto the end rail.
# {{lb|en|historical|billiards}} The buttons strung on a wire by which the score is kept.
# {{lb|en|billiards|by extension}} The points made in a game of billiards.
# {{lb|en|billiards|pool}} The line from behind and over which the [[cue ball]] must be played after being out of play, as by being pocketed or knocked off the table; also called the ''string line''.
# A strip, as of leather, by which the covers of a book are held together.
#* {{RQ:Milton Of Reformation|passage=Many of those that pretend to be great Rabbies in these studies have scarce saluted them from the '''strings''', and the titlepage.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A fibre, as of a plant; a little fibrous root.
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|passage=Duckweed putteth forth a little '''string''' into the water, from the bottom.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[nerve]] or [[tendon]] of an animal body.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Mark|7|35|passage=The '''string''' of his tongue was loosed.}}
# {{lb|en|carpentry}} A board supporting steps
#: {{syn|en|stringer|stringboard|stringpiece}}
# {{lb|en|shipbuilding}} An inside range of ceiling planks, corresponding to the [[sheer]] [[strake]] on the outside and bolted to it.
# {{lb|en|botany}} The tough fibrous substance that unites the [[valve]]s of the [[pericarp]] of [[leguminous]] [[plant]]s.
#: {{ux|en|the '''strings''' of beans}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A small, [[filamentous]] [[ramification]] of a [[metallic]] [[vein]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1833|author=Thomas Sopwith|title=An Account of the Mining Districts of Alston Moor, Weardale {{...}}|passage=a single miner is often found pursuing his solitary labours at a '''string''' or thin vein of ore}}
# {{lb|en|architecture|masonry}} A [[stringcourse]].
# {{lb|en|dated|slang}} A [[hoax]]; a [[fake]] [[story]].
# {{synonym of|en|stable||group of prostitutes managed by one pimp}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Steve Niles; Jeff Mariotte|title=30 Days of Night: Rumors of the Undead|page=307
|passage=They were turning tricks, doing drugs, and generally little better off than they had been before, except that they were keeping more of their money. But they seemed lonely, too, without the company of their pimp and the rest of his '''string'''.}}
# {{lb|en|oil drilling}} A column of [[drill pipe]] that transmits drilling fluid (via the [[mud pump]]s) and torque (via the [[kelly drive]] or [[top drive]]) to the [[drill bit]].

